#
#  DWD ICON global (R03B07, about 13 km) MODEL-LEVEL GRIB2 for the Rust
#  met_intermediate writer, map source "dwd".  Source: Deutscher Wetterdienst
#  (DWD), CC BY 4.0.  The pressure-level twin is Vtable.ICON-GLOBAL.rw, which
#  documents the surface and soil rows repeated here unchanged.
#
#  ICON's native GDT 3.101 mesh is not a lat-lon grid: these rows read the
#  regional regular lat-lon GRIB2 that gdt101_remap writes, which keeps each
#  object's product section.  GRIB2 only.
#
#  * Model levels are fixed-surface type 150 (generalized vertical height),
#    numbered from the model top: full levels 1..120 (T, QV, U, V, P, each
#    bounded by half levels k and k+1), half levels 1..121 (HHL, the
#    geometric height of each interface, published at step 0 only -- pass
#    it with --invariant and --invariant-field HHL for later leads).  Each
#    level is written at xlvl = its number.  A file mixing these with
#    pressure levels is refused.
#  * PRES is P, SPECHUMD is QV.  GHT is derived (rule ght_from_hhl) as the
#    mean of the two bounding half-level heights, (HHL(k) + HHL(k+1)) / 2;
#    a full level whose two half levels are not both present is refused.
#    The non-zero 3-D PRES is what selects the init's model-level branch.
#  * HHL has a blank description: read and consumed, never published.
